    "title": "Fiery crash shuts down I-81 South in Sullivan Co. - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kenzie Hagood Faith Little Slater Teague ,\n3 hours ago\nKINGSPORT, Tenn. (WJHL) — The southbound lanes are closed on Interstate 81 in Sullivan County after a multi-vehicle crash involving a fire near mile marker 60.\nAccording to the Tennessee Department of Transportation’s SmartWay map, the crash was reported at 9:54 p.m. just before the Fort Henry Drive exit.\nSilver Alert issued for man last seen at Kingsport hospital “We are currently on the scene of this incident and the investigating Troopers there are reporting that this is a serious crash that will take time to sort out,” the Tennessee Highway Patrol stated in a statement to News Channel 11.\nTDOT says traffic is being diverted at Exit 63, the Airport Parkway exit.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJHL | Tri-Cities News & Weather.\n2",
